      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important to clean and properly dress the wound to minimize infection risk. Wash your hands thoroughly and use an antiseptic wash on the wound with mild soap. Rinse it with clean water, then apply an antibiotic ointment; cover with a sterile bandage. Monitor the wound for signs of infection, like increased redness, swelling, or pus. If any of these occur or if the wound doesn't heal, seek medical attention. It’s best to prioritize health in the long run, even for minor injuries like this.",
